       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine in adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Higher doses add mainly peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually give little extra blood pressure lowering.\n\nWas this a typo, or is the dose intentional? Here are the options:\n\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose. I can enter it now if you confirm.\n- **20 mg as written.** If you want this, tell me it's intentional and give a short rationale. I'll enter it with a note saying the dose is above the usual maximum and was confirmed by you.\n- **Something else.** If the goal is more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide is usually preferred over going above 10 mg. I can enter that instead.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
